@page "/"

<PageTitle>Ruvents</PageTitle>

<section class="hero">
    <p class="hero-eyebrow">Family events · potlucks · RSVPs</p>
    <h1>Gather everyone, without the group-chat chaos.</h1>
    <p class="hero-lede">
        Create an event once, tell your whole family, and watch the RSVPs and
        potluck sign-ups fill in. No screenshots, no “who is bringing what?”
        threads, no lost details.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
        <AuthorizeView>
            <Authorized>
                <a class="button-primary" href="dashboard">Open your dashboard</a>
                <a class="button-secondary" href="groups">Your family groups</a>
            </Authorized>
            <NotAuthorized>
                <a class="button-primary" href="Account/Register">Create your account</a>
                <a class="button-secondary" href="Account/Login">I already have an account</a>
            </NotAuthorized>
        </AuthorizeView>
    </div>
</section>

<div class="feature-grid">
    <section>
        <h2>One shared calendar</h2>
        <p>
            Every event carries the details that matter: when, where, a map link,
            an RSVP deadline, and a cover image so it is instantly recognizable.
        </p>
    </section>
    <section>
        <h2>Everyone accounted for</h2>
        <p>
            Household members without accounts — like the kids — are marked
            attending right alongside you, and additional guests get their own names.
        </p>
    </section>
    <section>
        <h2>Potluck, sorted</h2>
        <p>
            Open sign-up on an event, pre-fill the slots you need, and let everyone
            claim a dish or add their own. You always see what is still missing.
        </p>
    </section>
    <section>
        <h2>Announcements with replies</h2>
        <p>
            Organizers post announcements; members comment and reply in a single
            tidy thread, so nothing important scrolls away.
        </p>
    </section>
</div>
